module

public import LeanPool.CompositionAlgebrasOverRings.Composition.NormClassification
public import LeanPool.CompositionAlgebrasOverRings.Composition.Reduced.Splitness
public import LeanPool.CompositionAlgebrasOverRings.Conic.QuadraticAlgebra

/-!
# Automorphisms are the unital norm equivalences (`GPR 23.4`)

A **unital norm equivalence** of conic algebras is a linear equivalence carrying `1` to `1` and the
norm to the norm (`GPR 23.1`); `Composition/NormClassification.lean` produces them from arbitrary
norm isometries (`GPR 23.3`) and shows they preserve trace, conjugation and squares (`GPR 23.2`).

`GPR 23.4` compares them with algebra isomorphisms in the two directions that are true.

**(a) Every isomorphism or anti-isomorphism is a unital norm equivalence, in every rank.** The
norm of a finitely generated projective conic algebra is intrinsic (`GPR 16.16`), so a unital
linear equivalence preserving squares has no choice but to preserve it. This is
`ConicAlgebra.norm_map_of_linearEquiv` for isomorphisms and
`ConicAlgebra.norm_map_of_linearEquiv_of_map_mul_rev` for anti-isomorphisms, recorded here for a
self-map as `ConicAlgebra.norm_map_of_automorphism`.

**(b) For quadratic algebras the converse holds.** A **quadratic algebra** is a unital algebra that
is finitely generated projective of constant rank two (`GPR 16.4`). The proof is `GPR`'s, and it
holds over an **arbitrary** commutative ring, with no LG, nontriviality, regularity, composition or
characteristic hypothesis. Multiplication in a conic algebra generated by `1` and one element `u`
has only the two structure constants `t(u)` and `n(u)` (`GPR 19.8`), and a unital norm equivalence
preserves both (`GPR 23.2`), so out of such an algebra it is automatically multiplicative. A
quadratic algebra need not be generated by one element, but multiplicativity is an equation, so it
may be checked after base change to the localization `k_𝔪` at every maximal ideal
(`ConicAlgebra.eq_of_forall_localization_maximal`), and a unital norm equivalence base changes to
one (`QuadraticMap.IsometryEquiv.baseChangeOfProjective`). Over `k_𝔪`, as over any LG ring, the
unit is unimodular (`GPR 16.7`) with a free complement of rank one (`GPR 11.24`), whose generator
`u` gives `k_𝔪 ⊗ A = k_𝔪[u]`
(`ConicAlgebra.exists_forall_mem_adjoinElement_of_isLGRing_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two`).

⚠ **(b) is false in higher rank**, which is why `GPR 23.4` is stated as it is. The standard
conjugation of a quaternion algebra is a unital norm equivalence — `ConicAlgebra.norm_conj` and
`ConicAlgebra.conj_one` — but it is an anti-automorphism, and a quaternion algebra is not
commutative (`ConicAlgebra.exists_mul_ne_mul_realQuaternion`). What rank two supplies is a property
of the algebra, not of the map.

## How the statement matches `GPR 23.4(b)`

`GPR 16.4` makes a quadratic algebra conic by Cayley–Hamilton, with `n(x) = det(L_x)` and
`t(x) = tr(L_x)`. The statements here instead take **arbitrary** conic structures `C` on `A` and
`D` on `B`. This loses nothing: a finitely generated projective algebra carries at most one conic
norm (`ConicAlgebra.norm_eq_of_projective`, `GPR 16.16`), so whatever conic structure is supplied,
its norm is the norm of `GPR 16.4`, and "`e` is a unital norm equivalence" means exactly what it
means in `GPR`. Only `A` is assumed finitely generated projective of constant rank two; for `B` this
follows from the linear equivalence, so `B` is only assumed to be conic. Neither algebra is assumed
associative or commutative; `GPR 16.4` shows both, but they are not needed here.

The existence half of `GPR 16.4` — every unital algebra that is finitely generated projective of
rank two admits a conic norm — is `ConicAlgebra.nonempty_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two`
(`Conic/QuadraticAlgebra.lean`). With it, `ConicAlgebra.map_mul_of_norm_map_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two`
states `GPR 23.4(b)` for quadratic algebras exactly as `GPR` does, with no conic structure
supplied.

## Main results

* `ConicAlgebra.norm_map_of_automorphism` : **`GPR 23.4(a)`**.
* `ConicAlgebra.map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_forall_mem_adjoinElement` : the engine of
  **`GPR 23.4(b)`** — a unital norm equivalence out of a monogenic conic algebra is multiplicative,
  over any commutative ring and with no regularity hypothesis.
* `ConicAlgebra.map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two` : **`GPR 23.4(b)`**.
* `ConicAlgebra.isomorphic_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two` : the same, as
  `ConicAlgebra.Isomorphic`.
* `ConicAlgebra.map_mul_iff_norm_map_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two` : **`GPR 23.4`** for quadratic
  algebras, both directions: a unital linear equivalence is multiplicative if and only if it
  preserves the norm.
* `ConicAlgebra.map_mul_of_norm_map_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two` : **`GPR 23.4(b)`** for quadratic
  algebras with their norms from `GPR 16.4`, no conic structure supplied.
* `ConicAlgebra.map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_finrank_eq_two`,
  `ConicAlgebra.map_mul_iff_norm_map_of_finrank_eq_two` : the field case, in dimension two.

## Implementation notes

Since mathlib's `AlgEquiv` requires associative multiplication, an automorphism is expressed
throughout as a `LinearEquiv` together with `map_one` and `map_mul`, exactly as in
`Composition/NormClassification.lean` and `Composition/Reduced/Splitness.lean`. No new predicate is
introduced.

## References

* [GPR] Garibaldi, Petersson, Racine, *Albert Algebras over Commutative Rings*, 11.24, 16.4, 16.7,
  16.16, 19.3, 19.8, 23.1--23.4.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v w

open scoped TensorProduct

namespace ConicAlgebra

variable {k : Type u} {A : Type v} [CommRing k] [NonAssocRing A] [Module k A]
  [SMulCommClass k A A] [IsScalarTower k A A] [Module.Finite k A] [Module.Projective k A]
  {B : Type w} [NonAssocRing B] [Module k B] [SMulCommClass k B B] [IsScalarTower k B B]

/-! ### `GPR 23.4(a)`: isomorphisms are unital norm equivalences -/

omit [SMulCommClass k A A] [IsScalarTower k A A] in
/-- **`GPR 23.4(a)`.** Every automorphism of a finitely generated projective conic algebra is a
unital norm equivalence: it preserves the norm, and hence the trace and the conjugation.

This is the self-map case of `ConicAlgebra.norm_map_of_linearEquiv`, and it holds in every rank
and over every commutative ring, because the conic norm on such an algebra is intrinsic
(`GPR 16.7`, `GPR 19.3`). -/
theorem norm_map_of_automorphism (C : ConicAlgebra k A) (e : A ≃ₗ[k] A)
    (map_one : e (1 : A) = 1) (map_mul : ∀ x y, e (x * y) = e x * e y) (x : A) :
    C.norm (e x) = C.norm x :=
  norm_map_of_linearEquiv C C e map_one map_mul x

/-! ### `GPR 23.4(b)`: in the monogenic case, unital norm equivalences are multiplicative -/

omit [Module.Finite k A] [Module.Projective k A] in
/-- **The engine of `GPR 23.4(b)`.** If every element of `A` lies in the quadratic subalgebra
`k[u]`, then every unital norm isometry out of `C` is multiplicative.

Multiplication in `k[u]` is the coefficient formula of `GPR 19.8`, whose only structure constants
are `t(u)` and `n(u)`; a unital norm isometry preserves the norm by hypothesis and the trace by
`GPR 23.2`, so it transports the formula. No regularity, projectivity, rank or characteristic
hypothesis is used. -/
theorem map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_forall_mem_adjoinElement (C : ConicAlgebra k A)
    (D : ConicAlgebra k B) (e : C.norm.IsometryEquiv D.norm) (h1 : e (1 : A) = 1) {u : A}
    (hu : ∀ x : A, x ∈ C.adjoinElement u) (x y : A) : e (x * y) = e x * e y := by
  have h := adjoinElementLinearEquivOfIsometryEquiv_map_mul C D e h1 u ⟨x, hu x⟩ ⟨y, hu y⟩
  exact congrArg (fun z : D.adjoinElement (e u) ↦ (z : B)) h

omit [Module.Finite k A] [Module.Projective k A] in
/-- **`GPR 23.4(b)`, as an isomorphism of conic algebras.** A unital norm isometry out of a
monogenic conic algebra is an isomorphism in the sense of `ConicAlgebra.Isomorphic`. -/
theorem isomorphic_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_forall_mem_adjoinElement (C : ConicAlgebra k A)
    (D : ConicAlgebra k B) (e : C.norm.IsometryEquiv D.norm) (h1 : e (1 : A) = 1) {u : A}
    (hu : ∀ x : A, x ∈ C.adjoinElement u) : C.Isomorphic D :=
  ⟨e, h1, map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_forall_mem_adjoinElement C D e h1 hu⟩

/-! ### `GPR 23.4(b)` for quadratic algebras -/

/-- **`GPR 23.4(b)`.** A unital norm equivalence from a quadratic algebra onto a conic algebra is
multiplicative, over an arbitrary commutative ring.

Here `A` is finitely generated projective of constant rank two, i.e. quadratic in the sense of
`GPR 16.4`; the target `B` need only be conic, since finite generation, projectivity and rank pass
to it along `e`. The conic structures are arbitrary, which is no loss: on a finitely generated
projective algebra the conic norm is unique (`ConicAlgebra.norm_eq_of_projective`), so it is the
norm `det(L_x)` of `GPR 16.4`.

Following `GPR`, the equation is checked at each localization `k_𝔪`, where `k_𝔪 ⊗ A = k_𝔪[u]`
(`ConicAlgebra.exists_forall_mem_adjoinElement_of_isLGRing_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two`) and
multiplication in `k_𝔪[u]` is determined by `t(u)` and `n(u)` (`GPR 19.8`), both preserved by a
unital norm equivalence (`GPR 23.2`). -/
theorem map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two (C : ConicAlgebra k A)
    (D : ConicAlgebra k B) (hA : Module.rankAtStalk (R := k) A = fun _ ↦ 2)
    (e : C.norm.IsometryEquiv D.norm) (h1 : e (1 : A) = 1) (x y : A) : e (x * y) = e x * e y := by
  have : Module.Finite k B := Module.Finite.equiv e.toLinearEquiv
  have : Module.Projective k B := Module.Projective.of_equiv' e.toLinearEquiv
  refine eq_of_forall_localization_maximal (k := k) _ _ fun P _ ↦ ?_
  let S := Localization.AtPrime P
  have hSrank := Module.rankAtStalk_baseChange_of_eq S hA
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := (C.baseChangeOfProjective S)
    |>.exists_forall_mem_adjoinElement_of_isLGRing_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two
      (isLGRing_of_isLocalRing S) hSrank
  let eS := QuadraticMap.IsometryEquiv.baseChangeOfProjective (A := S) C.norm D.norm e
  have h1S : eS (1 : S ⊗[k] A) = 1 := congrArg ((1 : S) ⊗ₜ[k] ·) h1
  have h := map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_forall_mem_adjoinElement
    (C.baseChangeOfProjective S) (D.baseChangeOfProjective S) eS h1S hu (1 ⊗ₜ x) (1 ⊗ₜ y)
  rw [← one_tmul_mul] at h
  exact h.trans (one_tmul_mul S (e x) (e y)).symm

/-- **`GPR 23.4(b)`, as an isomorphism.** A unital norm equivalence from a quadratic algebra onto a
conic algebra is an isomorphism of conic algebras, over an arbitrary commutative ring. -/
theorem isomorphic_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two (C : ConicAlgebra k A)
    (D : ConicAlgebra k B) (hA : Module.rankAtStalk (R := k) A = fun _ ↦ 2)
    (e : C.norm.IsometryEquiv D.norm) (h1 : e (1 : A) = 1) : C.Isomorphic D :=
  ⟨e, h1, map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two C D hA e h1⟩

/-- **`GPR 23.4` for quadratic algebras, both directions.** Let `A` be finitely generated
projective of constant rank two and `e : A ≃ₗ[k] B` a linear equivalence with `e 1 = 1`. Then `e`
is multiplicative if and only if it carries the norm of `C` to the norm of `D`.

Forwards is `GPR 23.4(a)` (`ConicAlgebra.norm_map_of_linearEquiv`) and holds in every rank;
backwards is `GPR 23.4(b)`, where rank two is used. -/
theorem map_mul_iff_norm_map_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two (C : ConicAlgebra k A) (D : ConicAlgebra k B)
    (hA : Module.rankAtStalk (R := k) A = fun _ ↦ 2) (e : A ≃ₗ[k] B) (h1 : e (1 : A) = 1) :
    (∀ x y, e (x * y) = e x * e y) ↔ ∀ x, D.norm (e x) = C.norm x :=
  ⟨fun hmul x ↦ norm_map_of_linearEquiv C D e h1 hmul x, fun hnorm ↦
    map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two C D hA
      { toLinearEquiv := e, map_app' := hnorm } h1⟩

/-- **`GPR 23.4(b)` for quadratic algebras as `GPR 16.4` defines them**: unital algebras that are
finitely generated projective of constant rank two, each with its conic norm — which exists by
`GPR 16.4` (`ConicAlgebra.ofRankTwo`) and is unique by `GPR 16.16`
(`ConicAlgebra.eq_ofRankTwo`). A unital norm equivalence between them is an algebra isomorphism;
no conic structure needs to be supplied. -/
theorem map_mul_of_norm_map_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two [Module.Finite k B] [Module.Projective k B]
    (hA : Module.rankAtStalk (R := k) A = fun _ ↦ 2)
    (hB : Module.rankAtStalk (R := k) B = fun _ ↦ 2) (e : A ≃ₗ[k] B) (h1 : e (1 : A) = 1)
    (hnorm : ∀ x, (ofRankTwo hB).norm (e x) = (ofRankTwo hA).norm x) (x y : A) :
    e (x * y) = e x * e y :=
  map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two (ofRankTwo hA) (ofRankTwo hB) hA
    { toLinearEquiv := e, map_app' := hnorm } h1 x y

/-! ### The field case -/

section Field

variable {K : Type u} {X : Type v} {Y : Type w} [Field K]
  [NonAssocRing X] [Module K X] [SMulCommClass K X X] [IsScalarTower K X X]
  [Module.Finite K X] [Module.Projective K X]
  [NonAssocRing Y] [Module K Y] [SMulCommClass K Y Y] [IsScalarTower K Y Y]

/-- **`GPR 23.4(b)` over a field.** A unital norm isometry out of a two-dimensional conic algebra
over a field is multiplicative. -/
theorem map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_finrank_eq_two (E : ConicAlgebra K X)
    (F : ConicAlgebra K Y) (hX : Module.finrank K X = 2) (e : E.norm.IsometryEquiv F.norm)
    (h1 : e (1 : X) = 1) (x y : X) : e (x * y) = e x * e y :=
  map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two E F
    (Module.rankAtStalk_eq_of_finrank_eq hX) e h1 x y

/-- **`GPR 23.4(b)` over a field, as an isomorphism.** -/
theorem isomorphic_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_finrank_eq_two (E : ConicAlgebra K X)
    (F : ConicAlgebra K Y) (hX : Module.finrank K X = 2) (e : E.norm.IsometryEquiv F.norm)
    (h1 : e (1 : X) = 1) : E.Isomorphic F :=
  ⟨e, h1, map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_finrank_eq_two E F hX e h1⟩

/-- **`GPR 23.4` over a field, both directions.** A unital linear equivalence out of a
two-dimensional conic algebra over a field is multiplicative if and only if it preserves the norm.
-/
theorem map_mul_iff_norm_map_of_finrank_eq_two (E : ConicAlgebra K X) (F : ConicAlgebra K Y)
    (hX : Module.finrank K X = 2) (e : X ≃ₗ[K] Y) (h1 : e (1 : X) = 1) :
    (∀ x y, e (x * y) = e x * e y) ↔ ∀ x, F.norm (e x) = E.norm x :=
  map_mul_iff_norm_map_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two E F (Module.rankAtStalk_eq_of_finrank_eq hX) e h1

end Field

end ConicAlgebra
